{# THE TOP RUNG — the page frame, and the reason this bundle exists.

   A module page extends THIS and fills sockets. It types no furniture: no
   `<div class="page">`, no crumb markup, no flash loop of its own. Before the
   shell, every module carried a copy of all three, and a change to the
   frame reached the copies somebody remembered.

   THE VERTICAL ORDER IS PART OF THE CONTRACT — trail, page head, tabs, flashes,
   body — because a module filling shell_page_actions has to know its buttons
   land beside the title and above the tabs, or it will place them itself.

   AN UNFILLED SOCKET LEAVES NOTHING BEHIND. Every region below is captured
   first and rendered only if it has content, so a page with no subtitle gets no
   empty paragraph and no 24px gap it did not ask for. That is the difference
   between a frame you can trust and a frame every author reaches around. #}
{% extends '@Shell/shell.html.twig' %}

{% block content %}
    {%- set _crumbs %}{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}{% endblock %}{% endset -%}
    {%- set _title %}{% block shell_page_title %}{% endblock %}{% endset -%}
    {%- set _subtitle %}{% block shell_page_subtitle %}{% endblock %}{% endset -%}
    {%- set _actions %}{% block shell_page_actions %}{% endblock %}{% endset -%}
    {%- set _tabs %}
        {%- block shell_page_tabs -%}
            {# THE DEFAULT IS THE AREA SHELL, and that is the defect this fixes:
               today a module page inside an area loses the area's tabs entirely,
               because the strip lives in a partial the host includes by hand.
               Here a module page that fills only its body still shows you where
               you are. A page outside any place says so by saying nothing —
               fill this socket with nothing to opt out. #}
            {%- include '@Shell/_area_tabs.html.twig' with {tabs: shell_tabs()} only -%}
        {%- endblock -%}
    {% endset -%}
    {%- set _flashes %}
        {%- block shell_flashes -%}
            {# ONE FLASH MARKUP, RENDERED ONCE, BY THE FRAME. This block is
               overridable and a module overriding it is a bug report: before the
               shell, the host said "saved" one way, and two modules said
               it two other ways, each with its own class and its own tick. #}
            {%- include '@Shell/_flashes.html.twig' with {flashes: app.flashes} only -%}
        {%- endblock -%}
    {% endset -%}

    <div class="page">
        {%- if _crumbs|trim is not empty %}<div class="crumb">{{ _crumbs }}</div>{% endif -%}

        {%- set _head %}{% block shell_page_head %}
            {%- if _title|trim is not empty or _subtitle|trim is not empty or _actions|trim is not empty -%}
                <div>
                    {%- if _title|trim is not empty %}<h1 class="pg">{{ _title }}</h1>{% endif -%}
                    {%- if _subtitle|trim is not empty %}<p class="pgsub">{{ _subtitle }}</p>{% endif -%}
                </div>
                {%- if _actions|trim is not empty %}<div class="pgact">{{ _actions }}</div>{% endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {% endblock %}{% endset -%}
        {%- if _head|trim is not empty %}<div class="pghead">{{ _head }}</div>{% endif -%}

        {{- _tabs -}}
        {{- _flashes -}}

        <div class="pgbody">{% block shell_page %}{% endblock %}</div>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
